13.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B2}
White can initiate a kill by playing B2. B2 is the shared liberty of the three black groups that form the corner net, A2, B3-B4 and C1-C2. 

After B2 the black stones A2, B3 and C2 lose their last mutual breathing point. A2 is left with only A1 and A3, B3 is left with only A3 and the C1-C2 chain is left with only B1. Black cannot defend all three points at once and any attempt to connect, e.g. B2 is already occupied by White, means at least one of the groups is reduced to a single liberty which White can then take on the next move. The shape is therefore dead and B2 is the forcing starting point of the capture sequence.

