PRIVATE REFLECTION: {The board is the classic three-group corner net on A2, B3-B4 and C1-C2. The only points that touch the black liberties are A1, A3, A4, B1 and B2. W B1 puts C1-C2 in atari on B2 and gives W B1 the two liberties A1,B2. B B2 is the only useful defence and it joins A2,B3-B4,C1-C2 into the six stone mass M = A2 B2 B3 B4 C1 C2 with the three liberties A1,A3,A4 and W B1 is now in atari on A1. The net can then be forced on A3/A4:
3.W A4 4.B A1 captures W B1 and leaves M with the two liberties A3,B1 and W A4 alive on A5. 5.W A3 connects W A4 and removes A3 from M, leaving M with the single liberty B1 which cannot be played by Black – B B1 would be self-atari of the whole mass – so 6.W B1 captures M. The symmetric 3.W A3 4.B A1 5.W A4 gives the same net. W B2 first is at once met by B B1 which captures the B2 stone and restores two liberties to the C1-C2-B1 mass, W A3/A4 first are met by an immediate Black capture or a connecting B B2 and no forced capture follows, and A1 is suicide. Hence the only first move that initiates a forced killing sequence is the corner atari B1.}

