11.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The three black components are A2 {A1,A3,B2}, B3–B4 {A3,A4,B2} and C1–C2 {B1,B2}. The only first points that touch the black liberty set {A1,A3,A4,B1,B2} are A1,A3,A4,B1,B2. After a defence of the white D1–D2 group the corner is a classic net on B2. Playing B1 puts C1–C2 in immediate atari on B2 and gives the white B1 stone the two liberties A1,B2. Black cannot increase the liberties of C1–C2 without playing B2 and B2 after W B1 is a connecting move that unites A2,B3–B4,C1–C2 into the six-stone mass A2–B2–B3–B4–C1–C2 with the three outer liberties A1,A3,A4 and leaves W B1 in atari on A1. The mass is then reduced by A3/A4 and the net closes on A1/B1. No other first point forces the same unplayable-liberty atari; W B2 is answered by B B1, W A3 is answered by B A4 and W A4 is answered by B B2. The conventional forcing opening of the corner net is therefore the atari on C1–C2 at B1.

